    "reviewed_conclusions": [
      "All 82 frozen scope input hashes match disk; the scope identifies this exact source commit and all eight own formal pages.",
      "The two actual implementations and five Mark bindings are correctly separated: the force sword and force greatsword share .035/.04/.045/.05 per peril step, but use distinct formatter behavior and actual Mark routes.",
      "Peril step count is k=min(4,floor(current_peril/.20)); each wrapper held-slot gate applies the own tier override to the same conditional power-level key, replacing the .05 fallback rather than adding to it. No separate stepped_stat_buffs table or hit-triggered stack exists.",
      "The documented modifier is applied after the native weapon power-type curve as S_native*(1+q+k*p). Examples distinguish the power input from final HP damage, impact, and hit-mass outcomes and correctly account for pre-existing applicable modifier q.",
      "The RAW English and Traditional Chinese strings match the fixed localization resource and hash. The single-hand formatter shows the four-step maximum, while the greatsword formatter shows only per-step p despite the shared “Up to/最多” wording; the documented discrepancy and retained RAW are supported.",
      "Ordinary melee, push and follow-up, special Force Slash, sticky extra hits on only Obscurus Mk II and Deimos Mk IV, fixed-update/cache timing, cooling/venting, held-slot switching, and true unequip behavior are described with the limits supported by the actual binding and source proofs.",
      "The actual icon receipt is in scope and reports verified public bytes/hash and visual review; weapon compatibility and reverse associations are part of the frozen scope."
